(8895, 74, 50, 'JEAN HERSHOLT HUMANITARIAN AWARD', true, 'Arthur Hiller', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(8896, 74, 48, 'HONORARY AWARD', true, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To Sidney Poitier in recognition of his remarkable accomplishments as an artist and as a human being.'),
(8897, 74, 48, 'HONORARY AWARD', true, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To Robert Redford: Actor, director, producer, creator of Sundance, inspiration to independent and innovative filmmakers everywhere.'),
(8898, 74, 47, 'GORDON E. SAWYER AWARD', true, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Edmund M. Di Giulio'),
(8899, 74, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, 'Sound', 'The work of John M. Eargle, D.B. \"Don\" Keele and Mark E. Engebretson has resulted in the over 20-year dominance of constant-directivity, direct radiator bass style cinema loudspeaker systems.', 'To JOHN M. EARGLE, D.B. \"DON\" KEELE and MARK E. ENGEBRETSON for the concept, design and engineering of the modern constant-directivity, direct radiator style motion picture loudspeaker systems.'),
(8900, 74, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, 'Lenses and Filters', 'This compact, wide-angle, macro focus lens enhances and expands the picture-capturing ability, both technically and artistically, of the cinematographer. It is the first cine lens that allows macro photography while still being able to zoom.', 'To IAIN NEIL for the concept and optical design and AL SAIKI for the mechanical design of the Panavision Primo Macro Zoom Lens (PMZ).'),
(8901, 74, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, 'Special Photographic', 'The ARRILASER film recorder demonstrates a high level of engineering resulting in a compact, user-friendly, low-maintenance device while at the same time maintaining outstanding speed, exposure ratings and image quality.', 'To FRANZ KRAUS, JOHANNES STEURER and WOLFGANG RIEDEL for the design and development of the ARRILASER Film Recorder.'),
(8902, 74, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, 'Laboratory', 'This photo-chemical process restores color to faded color negative using off-the-shelf film stocks with a unique approach. The resulting film intermediate can be used to create a new internegative.', 'To PETER KURAN for the invention, and SEAN COUGHLIN, JOSEPH A. OLIVIER and WILLIAM CONNER for the engineering and development of the RCI-Color Film Restoration Process.'),
(8903, 74, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, 'Special Photographic', 'This liquid-gate optical printer offers ease of set-up and change-over to various formats from 35mm to 65mm 15-perf with both additive and subtractive lamp houses.', 'To MAKOTO TSUKADA, SHOJI KANEKO and the TECHNICAL STAFF OF IMAGICA CORPORATION, and DAIJIRO FUJIE of Nikon Corporation for the engineering excellence and the impact on the motion picture industry of the Imagica 65/35 Multi-Format Optical Printer.'),
(8904, 74, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, 'Sound', 'Allowing all four soundtrack systems to be exposed on a single negative with relative ease, this stock has allowed single inventory prints, facilitating the more economic distribution of motion pictures.', 'To STEVEN GERLACH, GREGORY FARRELL and CHRISTIAN LURIN for the design, engineering and implementation of the Kodak Panchromatic Sound Recording Film.'),
(8905, 74, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, 'Special Photographic', 'CELCO recorder products have had a significant impact on the industry through continual improvements in their technology.', 'To PAUL J. CONSTANTINE and PETER M. CONSTANTINE for the design and development of the CELCO Digital Film Recorder products.'),
(8906, 74, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Photography', 'The Remote AquaCam brings to the industry an underwater camera housing specifically designed for remote and high-speed operation. Its hydro-dynamic shape facilitates ease of operation for surface hand-held filming, and its remote capabilities allow it to film in confined areas or in situations where an operator cannot be near the camera.', 'To PETE ROMANO for the design and development of the Remote AquaCam, an underwater camera housing system for use in motion pictures.'),
(8907, 74, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Photography', 'With over 50 years of involvement in the design and development of underwater camera housings, Jordan Klein''s work has had significant influence in the field of underwater photography.', 'To JORDAN KLEIN for his pioneering efforts in the development and application of underwater camera housings for motion pictures.'),
(8908, 74, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Sound', 'Employing both tapered line array and filtered line array technologies and unique passive and active filter networks, their work with cinema loudspeakers was both innovative and dedicated specifically to cinema applications.', 'To BERNARD M. WERNER and WILLIAM GELOW for the engineering and design of filtered line arrays and screen spreading compensation as applied to motion picture loudspeaker systems.'),
(8909, 74, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Sound', 'For over 20 years Tomlinson Holman has been involved in the research and integration of the constant-directivity, direct radiator bass type of cinema loudspeaker systems.', 'To TOMLINSON HOLMAN for the research and systems integration resulting in the improvement of motion picture loudspeaker systems.'),
(8910, 74, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Camera', 'This well-engineered camera motor features built-in time-lapse programmability and is useful in an unusually wide range of applications, including MOS production filming, high-speed photography, animation and motion control.', 'To GEOFF JACKSON and ROGER WOODBURN for their DMS 120S Camera Motor.'),
(8911, 74, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Camera Cranes', 'This motion control camera crane represents an unprecedented combination of long reach, high speed, and a novel approach to its transport, which allows a very rapid setup on location.', 'To THOMAS MAJOR BARRON for the overall concept and design; CHAS SMITH for the structural engineering; and GORDON SEITZ for the mechanical engineering of the Bulldog Motion Control Camera Crane.'),
(8912, 74, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'This system makes hair, clothing, skin, flesh and muscle simulation both directable and integrated within a character animation and rigging environment.', 'To JOHN R. ANDERSON, JIM HOURIHAN, CARY PHILLIPS and SEBASTIAN MARINO for the development of the ILM Creature Dynamics System.'),
(8913, 74, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'The MARS system provides analysis of camera motion and object motion, and their dimensions. It employs a rich set of user-interface tools and sophisticated algorithms.', 'To STEVE SULLIVAN and ERIC R.L. SCHAFER for the development of the ILM Motion and Structure Recovery System (MARS).'),
(8914, 74, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Special Photographic', 'CELCO recorder products have had a significant impact on the industry through continual improvements in their technology.', 'To CARL LUDWIG and JOHN M. CONSTANTINE, JR. for their contributions to CELCO Digital Film Recorder products.'),
(8915, 74, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'The Nuke-2D compositing software allows for the creation of complex interactive digital composites using relatively modest computing hardware.', 'To BILL SPITZAK, PAUL VAN CAMP, JONATHAN EGSTAD and PRICE PETHEL for their pioneering effort on the NUKE-2D Compositing Software.'),
(8916, 74, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'The ongoing influence of Lance Williams is exemplified in his three seminal papers \"Casting Shadows on Curved Surfaces,\" \"Pyramidal Parametrics\" and \"View Interpolation for Image Synthesis.\"', 'To DR. LANCE J. WILLIAMS for his pioneering influence in the field of computer-generated animation and effects for motion pictures.'),
(8917, 74, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'This dominant commercial tracking system provides \"survey-free\" tracking, which significantly reduces the need for painstaking, error-prone measurements on sets.', 'To DR. UWE SASSENBERG and ROLF SCHNEIDER for the development of \"3D Equalizer,\" an advanced and robust camera and object match-moving system.'),
(8918, 74, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'All current cel painting applications in the motion picture industry can be traced back to the original idea and pioneering implementation of Garland Stern.', 'To DR. GARLAND STERN for the concept and implementation of the Cel Paint Software System.'),
(8919, 74, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Stage Operations', 'This self-contained, low bed picture car carrier and camera platform enables the safe, economic and realistic filming of action sequences that may involve principal actors and dialogue.', 'To MIC RODGERS and MATT SWEENEY for the concept, design and realization of the \"Mic Rig.\"'),
(8920, 74, 46, 'AWARD OF COMMENDATION', true, NULL, NULL, 'The Super 16mm film format has achieved a significant impact on the worldwide film industry by playing a major role in empowering low budget films to be produced for theatrical release.', 'To Rune Ericson for his pioneering development and 30 years of dedication to the Super 16mm format for motion pictures.'),
(8921, 74, 46, 'AWARD OF COMMENDATION', true, NULL, NULL, 'Born from \"The Cinematographic Annual,\" first published by the ASC in 1930, the \"American Cinematographer Manual\" has become an essential bible for cinematographers. Currently in its eighth edition, this premier reference manual has had a significant impact on decades of motion picture photography around the world.', 'To the American Society of Cinematographers (ASC) for the continued publication of the \"American Cinematographer Manual.\"'),
(8922, 74, 51, 'JOHN A. BONNER MEDAL OF COMMENDATION', true, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To Ray Feeney in appreciation for outstanding service and dedication in upholding the high standards of the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences.'),
