(9035, 75, 48, 'HONORARY AWARD', true, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To Peter O''Toole, whose remarkable talents have provided cinema history with some of its most memorable characters.'),
(9036, 75, 60, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Academy Award of Merit)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'With its significant and dominant impact on the motion picture industry, the Maya software package offers a robust and widely used commercial visual effects tool with a rich infrastructure for extension and customization.', 'To ALIAS/WAVEFRONT for the development of a 3D animation, dynamics, modeling and rendering production tool known as Maya.'),
(9037, 75, 60, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Academy Award of Merit)', true, NULL, 'Camera', 'With a commitment that lies beyond the usual commercial considerations, these two manufacturers continue to lead the industry in developing and introducing products that have defined the state of the art in motion picture camera technology.', 'To ARNOLD & RICHTER CINE TECHNIK and PANAVISION INC., for their continuing development and innovation in the design and manufacturing of advanced camera systems specifically designed for the motion picture entertainment industry.'),
(9038, 75, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, 'Sound', 'This innovative design employs advanced hard disk recording technology and digital audio techniques for use in both production and post-production recording applications.', 'To GLENN SANDERS and HOWARD STARK of Zaxcom for the concept, design and engineering of the portable Deva Digital Audio Disk Recorder.'),
(9039, 75, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'Through a procedural building-block process, the Houdini software is used to simulate natural phenomena using particle effects and complex three-dimensional models.', 'To MARK ELENDT, PAUL H. BRESLIN, GREG HERMANOVIC and KIM DAVIDSON for their continued development of the procedural modeling and animation components of their Prisms program, as exemplified in the Houdini software package.'),
(9040, 75, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, 'Film', 'This film stock provides filmmakers with enhanced color saturation, higher contrast and darker blacks, producing a bold, colorful ''look'' on the theater screen.', 'To DR. LESLIE GUTIERREZ, DIANE E. KESTNER, JAMES MERRILL and DAVID NIKLEWICZ for the design and development of the Kodak Vision Premier Color Print Film, 2393.'),
(9041, 75, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, 'Lighting', 'This uniquely designed set light provides superior performance, reliability and ease of use. Combined with its excellent array of accessories, the Dedolight 400D is an outstanding engineering achievement.', 'To DEDO WEIGERT for the concept, DR. DEPU JIN for the optical calculations, and FRANZ PETTERS for the mechanical construction of the Dedolight 400D.'),
(9042, 75, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'This effective software simulation system is used to create and control natural, expressive, highly-nuanced facial animation on a wide range of computer-generated characters.', 'To DICK WALSH for the development of the PDI/DreamWorks Facial Animation System.'),
(9043, 75, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'Mental Ray is a highly programmable computer-graphics renderer incorporating ray tracing and global illumination to realistically simulate the behavior of light in computer-generated imagery.', 'To THOMAS DRIEMEYER and to the TEAM OF MATHEMATICIANS, PHYSICISTS AND SOFTWARE ENGINEERS OF MENTAL IMAGES for their contributions to the Mental Ray rendering software for motion pictures.'),
(9044, 75, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'The Deep Canvas software program captures the orginal brush strokes of the traditional background artist to render elements in three dimensions for animated films.', 'To ERIC DANIELS, GEORGE KATANICS, TASSO LAPPAS and CHRIS SPRINGFIELD for the development of the Deep Canvas rendering software.'),
(9045, 75, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Systems', 'The work of Jim Songer from 1968 through 1973 led directly to the more widespread acceptance of video-assist in the motion picture industry.', 'To JIM SONGER for his contributions to the technical development of video-assist in the motion picture industry.'),
(9046, 75, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Lighting', 'These helium-filled balloons with internal arrangements for tungsten halogen and HMI light sources, are usable indoors or out, quick to set up, require essentially no rigging and provide a soft light that can cover a very large area.', 'To PIERRE CHABERT of Airstar for the introduction of balloons with internal light sources to provide set lighting for the motion picture industry.'),
(9047, 75, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Lighting', 'These helium-filled balloons with internal arrangements for tungsten halogen and HMI light sources, are usable indoors or out, quick to set up, require essentially no rigging and provide a soft light that can cover a very large area.', 'To RAWDON HAYNE and ROBERT W. JEFFS of Leelium Tubelites for their contributions to the development of internally lit balloons for motion picture lighting.'),
(9048, 75, 51, 'JOHN A. BONNER MEDAL OF COMMENDATION', true, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To Curt R. Behlmer in appreciation for outstanding service and dedication in upholding the high standards of the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences.'),
(9049, 75, 51, 'JOHN A. BONNER MEDAL OF COMMENDATION', true, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To Richard B. Glickman in appreciation for outstanding service and dedication in upholding the high standards of the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences.'),
