(10065, 83, 48, 'HONORARY AWARD', true, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To Kevin Brownlow for the wise and devoted chronicling of the cinematic parade.'),
(10066, 83, 48, 'HONORARY AWARD', true, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To Jean-Luc Godard for passion. For confrontation. For a new kind of cinema.'),
(10067, 83, 48, 'HONORARY AWARD', true, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To Eli Wallach for a lifetime''s worth of indelible screen characters.'),
(10068, 83, 49, 'IRVING G. THALBERG MEMORIAL AWARD', true, 'Francis Ford Coppola', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(10069, 83, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'Dr. Sagar''s work led to a method for transforming facial motion capture data into an expression-based, editable character animation system that has been used in motion pictures with a high volume of digital characters.', 'To DR. MARK SAGAR for his early and continuing development of influential facial motion retargeting solutions.'),
(10070, 83, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, 'Stage Operations', 'The NAC System allows full-size cars, aircraft and other heavy props to be flown on wires with unprecedented freedom of motion and a high degree of safety, on-set and in real time. The intuitive control system responds to the motion of the operator''s hand, permitting the recording and playback of all axes of motion simultaneously, which may be edited and refined for playback in subsequent takes.', 'To MARK NOEL for the design, engineering, and development, and to JOHN FRAZIER for his contributions to the design and safety features, of the NAC Servo Winch System.'),
(10071, 83, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, 'Camera Cranes', 'The evolution of the Cablecam technology has made it possible to move a camera safely and accurately anywhere through a three-dimensional space.', 'To JAMES RODNUNSKY, ALEX MacDONALD and MARK CHAPMAN for the development of the Cablecam 3-D volumetric suspended cable camera technologies.'),
(10072, 83, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, 'Camera Cranes', 'The evolution of the Spydercam technology has made it possible to move a camera safely and accurately anywhere through a three-dimensional space.', 'To TIM DRNEC, BEN BRITTEN SMITH and MATT DAVIS for the development of the Spydercam 3-D volumetric suspended cable camera technologies.'),
(10073, 83, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'Mr. Ercolano''s work has been influential across the industry, and has enabled scalable render farms at numerous studios.', 'To GREG ERCOLANO for the design and engineering of a series of software systems culminating in the Rush render queue management system.'),
(10074, 83, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'This system was the first robust, scalable, widely adopted commercial solution for queue management in the motion picture industry. Its user interface and support for multi-machine assignment influenced the design of modern day queue management tools.', 'To DAVID M. LAUR for the development of the Alfred render queue management system.'),
(10075, 83, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'Queue was one of the first systems that allowed for statistical analysis and process introspection, providing a framework for the efficient use of render farms.', 'To CHRIS ALLEN, GAUTHAM KRISHNAMURTI, MARK A. BROWN and LANCE KIMES for the development of Queue, a robust, scalable approach to render queue management.'),
(10076, 83, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'ObaQ has scaled from managing a few hundred processors in 1997 to many thousands today, with minimal changes to the original design.', 'To FLORIAN KAINZ for the design and development of the robust, highly scalable distributed architecture of the ObaQ render queue management system.'),
(10077, 83, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Digital Imaging Technology', 'This important step in the evolution of global illumination techniques, first used on the motion picture \"Shrek 2,\" was shared with the industry in their technical paper \"An Approximate Global Illumination System for Computer Generated Films.\"', 'To ERIC TABELLION and ARNAULD LAMORLETTE for the creation of a computer graphics bounce lighting methodology that is practical at feature film scale.'),
(10078, 83, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, 'Systems', 'Easy to use, cineSync has become a widely accepted solution for remote production collaboration.', 'To TONY CLARK, ALAN ROGERS, NEIL WILSON and RORY McGREGOR for the software design and continued development of cineSync, a tool for remote collaboration and review of visual effects.'),
(10079, 83, 51, 'JOHN A. BONNER MEDAL OF COMMENDATION', true, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To Denny Clairmont in appreciation for outstanding service and dedication in upholding the high standards of the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences.'),
(10080, 84, 22, 'ACTOR IN A LEADING ROLE', false, 'Demián Bichir', 'Carlos Galindo', NULL, NULL);
