(11836, 96, 50, 'JEAN HERSHOLT HUMANITARIAN AWARD', true, 'Michelle Satter', NULL, NULL, NULL),
(11837, 96, 48, 'HONORARY AWARD', true, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To Angela Bassett, who has inspired audiences around the world with her powerful and fearless performances.'),
(11838, 96, 48, 'HONORARY AWARD', true, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To Mel Brooks, for his comedic brilliance, producing acumen and expansive body of work.'),
(11839, 96, 48, 'HONORARY AWARD', true, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To Carol Littleton, whose commitment to her craft has significantly elevated the art of film editing.'),
(11840, 96, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'Dolby Atmos has become an industry standard for object-based cinema audio content creation and presents a premier immersive audio experience for theatrical audiences.', 'To CHARLES Q. ROBINSON, NICOLAS TSINGOS, CHRISTOPHE CHABANNE, MARK VINTON and the TEAM OF SOFTWARE, HARDWARE AND IMPLEMENTATION ENGINEERS OF THE CINEMA AUDIO GROUP AT DOLBY LABORATORIES for the creation of the Dolby Atmos Cinema Sound System.'),
(11841, 96, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'Utilizing a novel optical mirror system, the IMAX Prismless Laser Projector removes prisms from the laser light path to create the high brightness and contrast required for IMAX theatrical presentation.', 'To STEVE READ and BARRY SILVERSTEIN for their contributions to the design and development of the IMAX Prismless Laser Projector.'),
(11842, 96, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'The Barco RGB Laser Projector''s novel and modular design with an internally integrated laser light source produces flicker-free uniform image fields with improved contrast and brightness, enabling a widely adopted upgrade path from xenon to laser presentation without the need for alteration to screen or projection booth layout of existing theaters.', 'To PETER JANSSENS, GORAN STOJMENOVIK and WOUTER D’OOSTERLINCK for the design and development of the Barco RGB Laser Projector.'),
(11843, 96, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'The Christie E3LH Dolby Vision Cinema Projection System utilizes a novel dual modulation technique that employs cascaded DLP chips along with an improved laser optical path, enabling high dynamic range theatrical presentation.', 'To MICHAEL PERKINS, GERWIN DAMBERG, TREVOR DAVIES and MARTIN J. RICHARDS for the design and development of the Christie E3LH Dolby Vision Cinema Projection System, implemented in collaboration between Dolby Cinema and Christie Digital engineering teams.'),
(11844, 96, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'For over a decade, OpenVDB''s core voxel data structures, programming interface, file format and rich tools for data manipulation continue to be the standard for efficiently representing complex volumetric effects, such as water, fire and smoke.', 'To KEN MUSETH, PETER CUCKA and MIHAI ALDÉN for the creation of OpenVDB and its ongoing impact within the motion picture industry.'),
(11845, 96, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'Marvelous Designer introduced a pattern-based approach to digital costume construction, unifying design and visualization and providing a virtual analogy to physical tailoring. Under Jaden Oh''s guidance, the team of engineers, UX designers and 3D designers at CLO Virtual Fashion has helped to raise the quality of appearance and motion in digital wardrobe creations.', 'To JADEN OH for the concept and development of the Marvelous Designer clothing creation system.'),
(11846, 96, 61, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Scientific and Engineering Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'USD is the first open-source scene description framework capable of accommodating the full scope of the production workflow across a variety of studio pipelines. Its robust engineering and mature design are exemplified by its versatile layering system and the highly performant crate file format. USD''s wide adoption has made it a de facto interchange format of 3D scenes, enabling alignment and collaboration across the motion picture industry.', 'To F. SEBASTIAN GRASSIA, ALEX MOHR, SUNYA BOONYATERA, BRETT LEVIN and JEREMY COWLES for the design and engineering of Pixar''s Universal Scene Description (USD).'),
(11847, 96, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'Bill Beck''s advocacy and education to the cinema industry while at Laser Light Engines contributed to the transition to laser projection in theatrical exhibition.', 'To BILL BECK for his pioneering utilization of semiconductor lasers for theatrical laser projection systems.'),
(11848, 96, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'At Novalux and Necsel, Gregory T. Niven demonstrated and refined specifications for laser light sources for theatrical exhibition, leading the industry''s transition to laser cinema projection technology.', 'To GREGORY T. NIVEN for his pioneering work in using laser diodes for theatrical laser projection systems.'),
(11849, 96, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'Yoshitaka Nakatsu, Yoji Nagao, Tsuyoshi Hirao, Tomonori Morizumi and Kazuma Kozuru collaborated closely with cinema professionals and manufacturers while at Nichia Corporation Laser Diode Division, leading to the development and industry-wide adoption of blue and green laser modules producing wavelengths and power levels matching the specific needs of the cinema market.', 'To YOSHITAKA NAKATSU, YOJI NAGAO, TSUYOSHI HIRAO, TOMONORI MORIZUMI and KAZUMA KOZURU for their development of laser diodes for theatrical laser projection systems.'),
(11850, 96, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'The roof pod improves the safety, speed and range of stunt driving, extending the options for camera placement while acquiring picture car footage with talent in the vehicle, leading to rapid adoption across the industry.', 'To ARNOLD PETERSON and ELIA P. POPOV for their ongoing design and engineering, and to JOHN FRAZIER for the initial concept of the Blind Driver Roof Pod.'),
(11851, 96, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'The unique and resilient design of this suite of pyrotechnic cable cutters has made them the preferred method for safe, precise and reliable release of suspension cables for over three decades in motion picture production.', 'To JON G. BELYEU for the design and engineering of Movie Works Cable Cutter devices.'),
(11852, 96, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'The HDE codec allows productions to leverage familiar and proven camera raw workflows more efficiently by reducing the storage and bandwidth needed for the increased amounts of data from high-photosite-count cameras.', 'To JAMES EGGLETON and DELWYN HOLROYD for the design, implementation and integration of the High-Density Encoding (HDE) lossless compression algorithm within the Codex recording toolset.'),
(11853, 96, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'Core engineering developments contributed by OpenVDB''s open-source community have led to its ongoing success as an enabling platform for representing and manipulating volumetric data for natural phenomena. These additions have helped solidify OpenVDB as an industry standard that drives continued innovation in visual effects.', 'To JEFF LAIT, DAN BAILEY and NICHOLAS AVRAMOUSSIS for the continued evolution and expansion of the feature set of OpenVDB.'),
(11854, 96, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'Atlas''s scene description and evaluation framework enables integration of multiple digital content creation tools into a coherent production pipeline. Its plug-in architecture and efficient evaluation engine provide a consistent representation from virtual production through to lighting.', 'To OLIVER CASTLE and MARCUS SCHOO for the design and engineering of Atlas, and to KEITH LACKEY for the prototype creation and early development of Atlas.'),
(11855, 96, 63, 'SCIENTIFIC AND TECHNICAL AWARD (Technical Achievement Award)', true, NULL, NULL, 'Alembic''s algorithms for storing and retrieving baked, time-sampled data enable high-efficiency caching across the digital production pipeline and sharing of scenes between facilities. As an open-source interchange library, Alembic has seen widespread adoption by major software vendors and production studios.', 'To LUCAS MILLER, CHRISTOPHER JON HORVATH, STEVE LaVIETES and JOE ARDENT for the creation of the Alembic Caching and Interchange system.'),
